/**
 * @mainpage meep-nw-simu-catalog
 *
 * @section intro Introduction
 *
 * **meep-nw-simu-catalog** (Go package `catalog`) is the Round 5.3
 * listing and instance helper for the ETSI MEC Sandbox. It talks to the
 * Network Emulator Manager (NEM) REST API on radio host **S** so the
 * sandbox UI can list Simu5G/OAI scenarios and create/delete NEM instances
 * without calling NEM from the browser.
 *
 * Module:
 * `github.com/InterDigitalInc/AdvantEDGE/go-packages/meep-nw-simu-catalog`
 *
 * Primary callers: `go-apps/meep-platform-ctrl` (`pcGetScenarioList`) and
 * `go-apps/meep-sandbox-ctrl` (`ceActivateScenario` / `ceTerminateScenario`).
 *
 * @section arch Architecture
 *
 * Two-host layout:
 * - Host **B** (MEC Sandbox): Kubernetes `meep-*`, including meep-platform-ctrl.
 * - Host **S** (radio emulator): NEM, default `http://172.29.10.20:8787`.
 *
 * Frontend contract is unchanged:
 * - `GET /platform-ctrl/v1/scenarios`
 * - `POST /{sbx}/sandbox-ctrl/v1/active/{name}`
 *
 * The browser never calls NEM. platform-ctrl uses this package when
 * `MEEP_NW_SIMULATOR_TYPE` is `simu5g` or `oai`.
 *
 * Listing flow:
 * 1. @ref FromEnv / @ref Config::UsesNem
 * 2. @ref Client::ListNemScenarios — `GET {nem-url}/v1/scenarios`
 * 3. CouchDB `GetDocList` (companions)
 * 4. @ref MergeNemWithCompanions
 * 5. `meep-model.JSONMarshallScenarioList`
 *
 * If step 2 fails, the handler returns **HTTP 502**. There is no CouchDB
 * fallback on the NEM path.
 *
 * Overlay pods on host B may not reach NEM on the node LAN. meepctl can
 * inject a host-network proxy and set `MEEP_NEM_URL` to
 * `http://<node.ip>:18787` while `repo.nw_simulator.nem-url` stays the
 * real NEM base URL.
 *
 * @section env Environment
 *
 * | Variable | Source in `.meepctl-repocfg.yaml` | Default |
 * |----------|-----------------------------------|---------|
 * | `MEEP_NW_SIMULATOR_TYPE` | `repo.nw_simulator.type` | `internal` |
 * | `MEEP_NEM_URL` | `repo.nw_simulator.nem-url` | empty |
 * | `MEEP_NEM_TIMEOUT_MS` | `repo.nw_simulator.timeout-ms` | `3000` |
 * | `MEEP_NEM_ACTIVATE_TIMEOUT_MS` | `repo.nw_simulator.activate-timeout-ms` | `180000` |
 *
 * Types:
 * - @ref TypeInternal — CouchDB listing; this package's NEM path is unused.
 * - @ref TypeSimu5G — NEM catalog (4G/5G Simu5G; WiFi PoA is not in this round).
 * - @ref TypeOAI — same NEM listing contract as simu5g.
 *
 * @section api Public API
 *
 * @subsection api_config Configuration
 * - @ref Config — type, NEM URL, timeout
 * - @ref FromEnv — load from process environment
 * - @ref Config::UsesNem — true for simu5g and oai
 * - @ref Config::Timeout — `time.Duration` for HTTP
 *
 * @subsection api_client NEM client
 * - @ref New — construct @ref Client
 * - @ref Client::Cfg
 * - @ref Client::ListNemScenarios — GET /v1/scenarios
 * - @ref Client::CreateInstance — POST /v1/instances (wait for READY)
 * - @ref Client::GetInstance — GET /v1/instances/{sandbox_id}
 * - @ref Client::DeleteInstance — DELETE /v1/instances/{sandbox_id}
 * - @ref NemScenario — `{id, description, bundle_dir}`
 * - @ref CreateInstanceRequest — `{sandbox_id, scenario_id, sim_time_limit}`
 * - @ref Instance — READY payload (`sandbox_id` is the instance-id)
 * - @ref IDSet — id set for filter matching
 *
 * @subsection api_merge Merge and filter
 * - @ref MergeNemWithCompanions — **listing path** (stubs for missing companions)
 * - @ref FilterCompanionDocs — companions only (NEM ids without YAML are dropped)
 *
 * @subsection api_errors Errors
 * - @ref ErrNemURLEmpty — `MEEP_NEM_URL` not set
 * - @ref ErrNemUnavailable — NEM down, HTTP error, or invalid JSON
 * - @ref ErrNemConflict — POST /v1/instances HTTP 409
 * - @ref ErrNemBadRequest — missing ids or HTTP 400
 *
 * Listing callers map URL/unavailable to HTTP 502. Test with `errors.Is`.
 *
 * @section merge_vs_filter Merge versus filter
 *
 * An empty JSON object `{}` is produced when `scenarios` is omitted
 * (`omitempty` on an empty slice). The frontend does
 * `if (!data.scenarios) return` and keeps a stale or empty listbox.
 *
 * @ref MergeNemWithCompanions always emits one document per NEM id so the
 * payload contains `"scenarios":[{name:...},...]`.
 *
 * Activate of a stub name POSTs NEM (`CreateInstance`) and skips virt-engine
 * until a CouchDB companion exists. That is expected when listing emitted a stub.

 *
 * @section usage Usage (platform-ctrl)
 *
 * @code{.go}
 * nwCfg := nwcat.FromEnv()
 * client := nwcat.New(nwCfg, nil)
 * if client.Cfg().UsesNem() {
 *     nemList, err := client.ListNemScenarios(r.Context())
 *     if err != nil {
 *         http.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadGateway)
 *         return
 *     }
 *     scenarioList = nwcat.MergeNemWithCompanions(nemList, scenarioList)
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section files Source files
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |------|------|
 * | doc.go | Package overview |
 * | config.go | Environment and @ref Config |
 * | client.go | NEM HTTP client (listing) |
 * | instance.go | NEM HTTP client (POST/GET/DELETE /v1/instances) |
 * | filter.go | Merge / filter helpers |
 * | catalog_test.go | Unit tests |
 *
 * @section build Generating this manual
 *
 * From `go-packages/meep-nw-simu-catalog`:
 * @code{.sh}
 * doxygen Doxyfile
 * @endcode
 * HTML output: `doxygen/html/index.html`.
 */
